content.text:
I spotted a weird expression in renderArtifacts: `rateFor(undefined, true)?.toFixed ? ...` — accidental. Need fix to `rateFor().toFixed(1)`. We'll fix later or now.

Also `renderWeapons` sets `owned ? 'equipped' : 'locked'` then adds equipped again; harmless but class "locked" for owned is wrong. Better class `${owned ? (equipped?'equipped':'') : 'locked'}`. We'll fix.

Now chunk 2 mechanics. Append after renderCodex closing. We need unique anchor: end of renderCodex `...`)}\n      ${tabs(...)}${body}`;\n  }` — we can anchor on final unique snippet.

Let's plan mechanics code with helper functions.

```js
  /* ---------------- MODALS & EFFECTS ---------------- */
  function openModal(symbol, eyebrow, title, text, actions) {...}
  function closeModal(){...}
  function tribulationEffect(success, text) {...}
```

`openModal` sets modalFields. Actions default.

Root:
```js
function weightedRoot() {
 const luck=luckFor();
 const weighted = rootTypes.map(r=>{
   const factor = {Common:1,Rare:1+luck*.025,Heavenly:1+luck*.07,Divine:1+luck*.1}[r.rarity]||1;
   return {r, w:r.weight*factor};
 });
 ...
}
```
`awakenRoot`, `rerollRoot`, `upgradeRoot`.

Meridian, Dao.

Breakthrough: `openBreakthrough`, `attemptBreak`.

Combat:
- `currentSpell`
- `rollStrike(base, opts)` returns {damage, crit, burn, evade?}. Actually implement damage calc.

Let's define:
```js
function calculateHit(base, s=state) {
  let dmg = base;
  let crit=false;
  if (Math.random() < critChance(s)) {
    const bonus = 1.5 + (daoLevel('sword',s)>=3 ? .25 : 0) + (equippedWeapon(s)?.id==='heavensedge' ? .35 : 0);
    dmg=Math.round(dmg*bonus); crit=true; s.stats.crit=(s.stats.crit||0)+1;
    if (daoLevel('lightning',s)>=3) s.qi += 4;
  }
  if (daoLevel('fire',s)>=3 && Math.random()<.2) dmg=Math.round(dmg*1.25);
  const w=equippedWeapon(s);
  if (w?.id==='emberfang' && Math.random()<.25 && w.awakened) dmg=Math.round(dmg*1.35);
  const comp=companionStrike();
  if (comp>0) dmg += comp;
  return {damage:Math.max(1,dmg), crit};
}
```
Maybe weapon ability only if awakened. Good.

`damageEnemy(base, source)`:
- if no enemy return.
- calculate hit; subtract; log message; if dead victory.
- else enemyRetaliate.
- save/render.
Need ensure state.enemy still exists after victory; don't retaliate.

`enemyRetaliate`:
```
let evaded = false;
if (daoLevel('space',3)>=3 && Math.random()<.15) evaded=true;
if (equippedWeapon()?.id==='mistfang' && Math.random()<.1) evaded=true;
if (evaded) toast; else {
 let taken = Math.max(1, enemy.damage - guardFor() - Math.floor(state.pathLevels.body/2));
